{"name":"Charmed","hex":"#ebcfc7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"charmed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Under a magic spell (cast by a charm); bewitched.","Having great good fortune, as though magically wrought."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of charm"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charmed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charmed","blocks":[{"text":"Charmed is an American fantasy drama television series created by Constance M. Burge and produced by Aaron Spelling and his production company Spelling Television, with Brad Kern serving as showrunner."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/af/Charmedtitlelogo1.jpg/330px-Charmedtitlelogo1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charmed","wikidata":"Q162371"},{"title":"Charmed (2018 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Charmed is an American fantasy drama television series developed by Jennie Snyder Urman, Jessica O'Toole, and Amy Rardin. It is a reboot of the WB series of the same name, created by Constance M. Burge, which originally aired from 1998 to 2006. Charmed premiered in the United States on October 14, 2018, on the CW. Carter Covington served as showrunner for the first season, before married duo Liz Kruger and Craig Shapiro took over for the second and third seasons. Jeffrey Lieber, Joey Falco, and Nicki Renna replaced Kruger and Shapiro as showrunners for the fourth season."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Charmed_%282018_TV_series%29_logo.svg/330px-Charmed_%282018_TV_series%29_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charmed_(2018_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q53162693"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/House_at_1329_Carroll_Ave.%2C_Los_Angeles_%28Charmed_House%29.JPG/500px-House_at